A final update...

I turned out to be (in Real Life) somewhat confused and inattentive...

A false key hit made me destroy my single wand of teleportation; at that
point I didn't worry too much, there are usually a lot in the dungeons.

After managing my dlvl 1 stash I killed the Wizard, levelported down to
the VS level - ...just to notice that I haven't yet located the Square!
Had to search *the whole* map (with the exception of the border paths)
until I finally got the strange vibrations.

Moloch was easy; with conflict and a rubber chicken corpse lying around
which was still fresh enough to kill the High Priest. Finally I escaped
the location with gain level.

The multiple double trouble Wizards have been a pain; I noticed far too
late that he was immune to my death ray. He stole everything from me;
the Amulet, Book, Bell, Candelabrum, and the Mirror of Merlin. And (for
the first time ever) I needed a lot of full healing during his attacks
and the attacks of his summoned minions.

Orcus' wand of death was the only one in the game and I needed a lot of
recharging for it.

Held down my the misterious force I have seen the levels 40-46 countless
times (as so often). But with all in all 6 cursed potions of gain level
I could finally escape Gehennom with all that recurring double troubling
Wizard. :-(

Took the saddle all the way with me for yet another horse to tame, until
Astral level... - but they died and died and died, and I often felt that
it was rarely worth the hassle.

Spell casting wasn't comfortable with that shield of reflection (which
was the only source of reflection; tons of different amulets but not the
good one).

The elemental planes were okay, with an orb(0:5) and a unique scroll of
gold detection that I found on my way up it did suffice exactly to find
the four portals.

But, on the Plane of Water. A kraken swung his arms around me; and I still
haven't found another wand of teleportation! (I didn't dare to think about
engraving the E-word in the air bubble within water.) Fortunately due to
the bubble movement I got released and took my wand of wishing (0:3) from
the castle (yet unused) to zap for a _wand of teleportation_; that was the
second wish in the game after some fountain incident with a water demon.
[Now that I think of it, I could have dropped a scroll of scare monster if
I'd have carried one in my inventory. I suppose that would have worked.]
Being a modest knight I wasn't disappointed that the wand of teleportation
was created with only 4 charges, I could recharge it if necessary.

At Astral I went for the mid altar, Famine. I feared that my wands will
get destroyed by lightning if I'd take off my shield of reflection to
cast magic missile, so I switched to enchant my 4 elven daggers (until
+6 as it turned out). I could kill Famine easily from distance with the
spell of magic missile, but the dragons and player characters and priests
were much tougher than usual. Finally my knight reached the chaotic altar.
Thinking about the options (helm of opposite alignment or struggle through
the troubles of all the tough creatures without enough charges in my wands
of death and teleportation) I finally realized that instead of his +6
Frostbrand he was still wielding the freshly enchanted daggers at basic
skill. Okay, that was the reason why the monsters were sooo hard to kill.

Nevermind. Too anxious that my real life sloppiness will kill this knight
he converted to chaos and offered the Amulet to his new god (who might or
might not provide him better support than his native god).

